## What We Are Building

The studio-machine's **C1 (creative readability) gate**. Root problem from the E02-vs-E03 analysis: E03 humor was unreadable because (a) genre bug kept GAGAD + genre-skills silent, (b) 22/24 videos ran plan-less, (c) Mode 4 auto-approved everything, (d) no critic judged storyboard *readability*. Fix stack (all SHIPPED + pushed to master, commit 9b5607e..c6fc100):
- Genre single-source (`genreForEpisode` reuses TD-59 code→UUID resolver) — wakes genre-filtered skills.
- **EXEC-CREAD** universal Creative Readability Critic (R01-R06 genre-neutral; genre rubric = swappable skill on shelf; HALT-without-paid-call if no playbook). Runs storyboard→CREAD→WCHK behind `READABILITY_GATE_ENABLED`.
- **T1 consolidation**: EXEC-GAGAD RETIRED (never worked in prod), its per-shot reviews absorbed into CREAD as eref/vanim phases. net −1598 LoC.
- C1 fanout gate: every fanout shot gets an animator plan; plan-less single-shot dies.
- New **cheap debug-tier providers**: `gemini-flash-image` (free) + `fal-wan` (Wan 2.6 Flash, $0.05/s).
- New `C1_STOP_BEFORE_EREF` verification kill-switch (halts Mode-4 after creative-text layer, before paid images).

---

## What WORKED (with evidence)

- **T1 GAGAD→CREAD consolidation** — confirmed: my independent verify trio tsc·0 / vitest 764/764 / replay-pilot 30/30; grep `EXEC-GAGAD|gag_plan|GagAssistant` → 0 files; live E06 run had **0 GAGAD jobs, 0 crashes**.
- **CREAD readability gate (live, the headline result)** — confirmed by E06 run on the REAL E02 brief: CREAD fired on the storyboard, verdict **REVISE** (passed R01,R03,R04,R05; failed R02 ×3 + R06), bounced STB→REVISION→Storyboarder re-author. Caught exactly the E03-class defects: missing **false-success beats** (R02: SH10-11 book-pyramid, SH18-19 mirror-smear, SH24-26 pillow-feather) + **empty kinetic motion** (R06: SH04 "wide grin, vibrating brush, churning sand, no goal-verb, no consequence"). Gave shot-level acceptance_criteria. `active-playbook check = true` → comedy skill (readability-comedy-slapstick) activated via genre fix.
- **C1_STOP_BEFORE_EREF flag** — confirmed: E06 reached storyboard/CREAD with **EREF = 0 jobs**, no image spend, $3.00 total on text layer.
- **gemini-flash-image provider (after fix)** — confirmed by live smoke: produced real 1024×1536 PNG, $0 free-tier, model `gemini-2.5-flash-image`.
- **fal-wan provider (produces video)** — confirmed by live smoke: real MP4 h264+aac, 5.0s, $0.25. BUT see aspect bug below.
- **Genre fix** — confirmed: comedy skill activated in CREAD on E06 (was dead in E03).

---

## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **gemini-flash-image shipped default model** — failed: `gemini-2.5-flash-preview-05-20` is a TEXT preview → API "not supported for generateContent". FIXED to `gemini-2.5-flash-image` (live-verified via ListModels), committed 4f84d6d.
- **fal-wan aspect_ratio** — failed: provider sends `aspect_ratio:'9:16'` but Wan schema has NO such param (only `resolution` 720p/1080p + image-derived aspect). Output came out **1440×1440 square**, not 9:16; provider also fabricates dims via `dimensionsFor()`. NOT yet fixed — flagged for decision (q45: fix provider vs use Seedance for real 9:16 + gemini-free for refs).
- **CREAD double-fire (live bug found in E06)** — CREAD ran TWICE on the same storyboard (two identical REVISE verdicts) → two parallel SB re-authors → revision-storm. Cause: storyboard approval fires CREAD via BOTH factory `isCriticChain` (exec-sb nextEvent) AND `computeNextEvents` STB branch; hasJob idempotency loses the race in the grace window. Bounded by cap+ceiling but wasteful. NOT fixed — needs a small dedup (pick one fire path).
- **Earlier E04 experiment** — abandoned: my stylized brief (not real E02) + late stop (after EREF started). Replaced cleanly by E06.

